This sample shows how to call GetMetadataConfigurationAsync.

Uri endpoint = new Uri("<endpoint>");
TokenCredential credential = new DefaultAzureCredential();
MetadataConfiguration client = new AttestationClient(endpoint, credential).GetMetadataConfigurationClient(apiVersion: "2025-06-01");

Response<OpenIDConfigurationResponse> response = await client.GetMetadataConfigurationAsync();

This sample shows how to call GetMetadataConfiguration.

Uri endpoint = new Uri("<endpoint>");
TokenCredential credential = new DefaultAzureCredential();
MetadataConfiguration client = new AttestationClient(endpoint, credential).GetMetadataConfigurationClient(apiVersion: "2025-06-01");

Response<OpenIDConfigurationResponse> response = client.GetMetadataConfiguration();

This sample shows how to call GetMetadataConfigurationAsync and parse the result.

Uri endpoint = new Uri("<endpoint>");
TokenCredential credential = new DefaultAzureCredential();
MetadataConfiguration client = new AttestationClient(endpoint, credential).GetMetadataConfigurationClient(apiVersion: "2025-06-01");

Response response = await client.GetMetadataConfigurationAsync(null);

JsonElement result = JsonDocument.Parse(response.ContentStream).RootElement;
Console.WriteLine(result.ToString());

This sample shows how to call GetMetadataConfiguration and parse the result.

Uri endpoint = new Uri("<endpoint>");
TokenCredential credential = new DefaultAzureCredential();
MetadataConfiguration client = new AttestationClient(endpoint, credential).GetMetadataConfigurationClient(apiVersion: "2025-06-01");

Response response = client.GetMetadataConfiguration(null);

